<title>FRANCE: France's Tapie shifted to jail near ailing father.</title>
<headline>France's Tapie shifted to jail near ailing father.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankrupt former French politician and soccer boss Bernard Tapie, serving an eight-month jail term for rigging a soccer match, is to be transferred from Paris to a prison in southern France to be close to his ailing father.</p>
<p>Prison service officials said on Friday Tapie would be moved to a jail, possibly in Marseille, closer to his father who has just had a heart attack. He would need special permission to visit his father. Tapie has been in jail since February 3.</p>
</text>
